# XSH dlopen()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Only the running program image and the objects it was started with are used: no shared object is built or
# assumed to exist. getpid() is the probe symbol, and the object that defines it is found with dladdr() and
# opened again by pathname. Flags other than the four defined are never passed.

assertion  XSH.dlopen.001
anchor     functions/dlopen.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/dlopen.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       dlopen(NULL, mode) returns a handle for the program image for each of
           RTLD_LAZY and RTLD_NOW combined with RTLD_GLOBAL and RTLD_LOCAL.
test       t/001-modes.c

assertion  XSH.dlopen.002
anchor     functions/dlopen.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       dlopen() of a pathname (containing a slash) that names no file returns
           a null pointer, and dlerror() then returns a diagnostic.
test       t/002-missing.c

assertion  XSH.dlopen.003
anchor     functions/dlopen.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       dlopen() of an existing file that is not an executable object returns
           a null pointer, and dlerror() then returns a diagnostic.
test       t/003-notobject.c

assertion  XSH.dlopen.004
anchor     functions/dlopen.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/dlopen.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       The object that defines getpid(), opened twice by its pathname with
           different modes, gives two handles through which dlsym() finds the
           same working getpid().
note       The page says only one copy of an object enters the address space
           however often it is opened. The handles themselves are not compared.
test       t/004-single-copy.c
